			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Daemon module\n\nThis commit applies strict code formatting and variable naming normalization to the `Source/Daemon/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting struct fields within `DaemonManager`, `PlatformInfo`, and `DaemonStatus` from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `pid_file_path` -> `PidFilePath`, `is_running` -> `IsRunning`).\n- Updating struct field initializations and internal references to reflect the capitalized naming convention.\n\nThis ensures the `Daemon` module, responsible for managing the lifecycle and status of the Air daemon process, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
			"SHA": "f6e94718c90fcb4ba98b229fc6c71dc0649ccba8"
