			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Configuration module\n\nThis commit applies strict variable naming normalization to the `Source/Configuration/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting local variables within the test module from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `dev_config` -> `DevConfig`, `home` -> `Home`).\n- Updating assertions and references to reflect the capitalized naming convention.\n\nThis ensures the `Configuration` module, responsible for managing application settings, profiles, and path expansion, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
			"SHA": "98346612a414e870ea5163da39e0f837c9acbf70"
