				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Binary module\n\nThis commit removes the `#![allow(non_snake_case, non_camel_case_types)]` lint waiver from the top of `Source/Binary.rs`.\n\nWith this suppression removed, the Rust compiler will now strictly enforce naming conventions for variables and types within the Binary module. This change aligns `Binary.rs` with the broader code hygiene standardization recently applied to other Air subsystems (Daemon, Downloader, ApplicationState, Authentication), ensuring consistent style and minimizing visual noise across the codebase.",
			"SHA": "0b31d544a6f0a65a9313febd79df347ee552f3b2"
