				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Air): Enforce code formatting in Authentication module\n\nThis commit applies strict code formatting and variable naming normalization to the `Source/Authentication/mod.rs` file, continuing the hygiene standards enforced across the Air codebase in recent commits.\n\nSpecific adjustments include:\n- Converting all function arguments and local variables from `snake_case` to `PascalCase` (e.g., `username` -> `Username`, `credentials_store` -> `CredentialsStore`).\n- Updating method signatures and internal calls to reflect PascalCase naming (e.g., `authenticate_user` -> `AuthenticateUser`, `generate_session_token` -> `GenerateSessionToken`).\n- Modifying utility calls and struct field initialization to align with the capitalized naming convention.\n\nThis ensures the `Authentication` module, responsible for user login, session management, and credential encryption within the Air daemon, adheres to the project's consistent style guide, minimizing visual noise in future diffs.",
			"SHA": "c4dbff0381779a1395c3eb63b7952e86abc64abe"
